@flexiarg baldwin/metaca-negative-evidence-localizes-the-bottleneck
@title MetaCA Negatives Localize Missing Baldwin Preconditions
@sigils [🔃/力]
@keywords negative-result, metaca, hold, dependence, mutation, evidence, diagnosis
@audience MetaCA researchers, experimental reviewers
@tone evidence-calibrated
@style pattern
@childof baldwin/mechanism
@references [baldwin/assimilable-traits-need-heritable-shadows baldwin/assimilation-requires-a-resolved-path baldwin/stationarity-decides-what-can-be-fixed]

! conclusion:
  Read the existing MetaCA runs as evidence that the tested hold representation and
  operators do not supply a selectable route to complete static replacement within the
  tested budget—not as evidence against Baldwinian guidance or genetic assimilation in
  other representations.

  + context:
    The corrected hold-only battery, path probe, static-search arm, and preregistered
    two-by-two pilot now expose distinct parts of the failure rather than one omnibus
    null.

  + IF:
    The result records and their limitations are interpreted together.

  + HOWEVER:
    Earlier claims were repeatedly invalidated by a read-mask that did not stop
    rewriting, an HGT operator that omitted hold bits, a mutation expectation with the
    wrong lifecycle, a cost axis whose ranking was inert, and endpoint claims inferred
    from random fields. The latest pilot still uses one evolution seed and thirty
    generations, so it is a pilot diagnosis rather than a population-level impossibility result.

  + THEN:
    Preserve the following bounded findings: selection sustains high functional reach;
    successful genomes remain strongly rewrite-dependent; random hold substitutions
    are usually harmful; one locally selectable extra hold was found but the greedy
    path stopped immediately afterward; fixed-p0 and coupled random replacement did not
    produce a registered witness; and static evolutionary search did not discover the
    known distant endpoint in thirty generations.

  + BECAUSE:
    These observations agree on a specific causal diagnosis: plastic rewriting is
    currently the expressed functional mechanism, while the inherited bytes exposed by
    holding are neither prepared substitutes nor connected to the distant static
    solutions by a resolved local gradient.

    + EVIDENCE:
      The search pilot's four selected arms end at mean reach 12.4389--12.9972,
      dependence 0.9609--0.9844, and held fraction 0.0156--0.0391, with outcome
      `:no-tested-repair`. The hold-only static-search arm ends at reach 1.1778. The
      greedy path records one selected step and then `:no-selectable-step`.

    + COUNTERFACTUAL:
      A prepared, partially expressed inherited shadow that becomes enriched before
      holding would contradict the representation diagnosis. Faster early learning
      under evolved inherited fields would establish Baldwinian guidance even if the
      strict static witness continued to fail.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - Attach future results to the precise gate they test.
    - Do not aggregate corrected and invalidated historical arms into one effect size.
